git status
- It tells the current state of the project from Git's perspective

git init
- Initializes the folder as a Git repository

♠ Git doesn't track empty folders
- The green color indicates from VS code that these are new files that git hasn't started tracking yet
- U means Untracked

git branch -M main
git branch - it is the git command for working with branches
main
 │
 ├── development
 │
 └── security-feature

 - We'll work with main initially and later we can separate branches for bigger Pulse Net features

 -M - it means rename (force if needed) the current branch

 ♦ Modern github repository generally uses main instead of Master



 New-Item .gitignore -ItemType File
 - That creates .gitignore directly in the current Pulse Net directory, regardless of what you have selected in the Explorer

 ♠ .gitignore
 - This file tells Git don't upload or track these files
 - These can contain huge dependency folders, generated files, or sensitive credentials.